<ArticleLayout slug="youtube-video-thumbnail-specs" ctaLabel="Create your account" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">YouTube now recommends custom thumbnails at 3840 by 2160 pixels, three times the width most spec sheets still print. Before the pixels matter, though, the account has to qualify: no phone verification, no custom thumbnail.</p>

  <p>Reviewed October 8, 2026. Every spec below is read from YouTube's own help pages, and each row names the page it came from.</p>

  <h2>What is the YouTube thumbnail size in 2026?</h2>

  <p>YouTube recommends 3840 by 2160 pixels for a video thumbnail: 16:9, at least 640 pixels wide, as JPG or PNG. The file can weigh up to 50MB from a computer but only 2MB from a phone, and only a phone-verified account can upload one. In hubStudio, you render it in the Image studio and crop it in the Image editor.</p>

